{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288458-what-breaks-if-there-is-a-declaration-phase-for-damage","id":1288458,"title":"What Breaks if there is a Declaration Phase for damage?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-15T18:10:34-08:00","id":1288458,"title":"What Breaks if there is a Declaration Phase for damage?","content":"So, as I understand it (and I might be wrong), the way it goes in combat now is:<br /> <br /> 1. Attacker declares all Attack and Damage boosters<br /> 2. Defender declares all dodge/parry and soak boosters<br /> 3. Resolution<br /> <br /> But I have found in my limited experience that this tends to err on a lot of premature charm activation. After all, why activate your entire damage suite if you whiffed? Or your soak everything ability when the Daiklaive misses your head by miles?<br /> <br /> So I'm just wondering if any of the game's mechanics break down if you can:<br /> <br /> 1. Attacker Declares all Attack Boosters<br /> 2. Defender declares all dodge/parry boosters<br /> 3. Hit determined, if hit goto 4<br /> 4. Attacker declares all damage boosters<br /> 5. Defender declares all soak boosters/damage mitigators<br /> <br /> I know it makes damage and soak charms more powerful, but I feel like that since it is the same advantage for both attacker and defender, it makes not so much difference?<br /> <br /> Hmmm...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T18:53:40-08:00","id":1288472,"title":"","content":"I think we already play it your way at my table. Unsure if that's wrong or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T19:00:01-08:00","id":1288475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288458-what-breaks-if-there-is-a-declaration-phase-for-damage?p=1288472#post1288472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we already play it your way at my table. Unsure if that's wrong or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hows it play? Too fiddly? Damage and soak charms become too powerful?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T19:11:27-08:00","id":1288484,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1288458-what-breaks-if-there-is-a-declaration-phase-for-damage?p=1288475#post1288475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hows it play? Too fiddly? Damage and soak charms become too powerful?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have anything to compare it to but it seems fine for us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T19:17:14-08:00","id":1288487,"title":"","content":"From my understanding the soak charms are balanced around the fact they have to be activated before a hit unless stated otherwise.<br /> <br /> This change will make any soak/resistance build a lot stronger but I am not sure if it will be a problem in any particular game.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T19:46:15-08:00","id":1288497,"title":"","content":"From my experience this punishes those who have invested in dodge as a method of defence. As they need to treat any attack as a serious threat least the attack manages to hit and then they decide to invest motes in damage charms. Although it is certainly easier from a game flow perspective as it allows people to just worry about the attack roll, then worry about the damage roll. While players are getting use to the game I would generally allow retroactive activation of damage charms as it is a lot to take in initially.<br /> <br /> For example knowing if that Nephwrack is using soul destruction on you may encourage you to burn motes to make sure he misses. However if you change the declaration order it enables the GM to avoid letting the players know that this attack even exists until an attack roll succeeds. Part of the importance of this declaration is so the players know the consequences of the roll so they as a player can make an informed decision on mote expenditure. Essentially this opens the door for the GM to hide what the failure outcome of a roll is, which while appropriate for a horror setting it isn't exactly what exalted is portrayed as.<br /> <br /> Also there would be a significant balance ramification between simple charms that enhance damage vs supplemental charms that enhance damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5167-klaek","name":"Klaek","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T20:01:19-08:00","id":1288503,"title":"","content":"Keeping offense and defense grouped means less pressure to invest in damage AND accuracy (or defense AND soak). If you split them, doing both becomes practically mandatory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T21:01:04-08:00","id":1288510,"title":"","content":"So this was how things were done in 2e and ended up creating what was sometimes called a 2-7 split or 2-7 filter after the declare dodge and declare soak phases. As a matter of fact, it didn't end up actually devaluing DVs that much, since the soak wouldn't save you from badtouch effects.<br /> <br /> However what it did do was let every player know if there was a scary bad-touch coming and if there wasn't they would just use the DV to see if the attack whiffed, and use the soak if it didn't and looked to pose a threat. It was not a good design space to be in since it made defense so much more efficient than offense. In an era without so many dangerous riders on attacks (at least until Sidereals come out), this might just result in hyper-efficient defense again, but even moreso this time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23919-nabirius","name":"Nabirius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T02:29:54-08:00","id":1288550,"title":"","content":"It makes mortals and other characters without a dice adder matter a bit less.<br /> Since now the overconfident Exalt who got hit is able to activate charms that could negate the whole thing or make them better of than if they'd just dodged/parried in the first place i.e. Iron Kettle Body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T07:57:04-08:00","id":1288598,"title":"","content":"Also some charms lose their cool unique exception, like Impervious Skin of Stone, which in Earth Aura can explicitly be used after an attack lands but before damage is rolled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T08:44:27-08:00","id":1288605,"title":"","content":"Hmm, looking at it again, I think I glossed over the part where Soak charms were declared separately. I think what I'm thinking of are instances where damage and soak charms are explicitly allowed to be declared after the fact, not specifically that we as a group <i>stop</i> to ask if people have anything to declare at that point. Mild rollback of my statement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T12:46:15-08:00","id":1288692,"title":"","content":"It also makes certain charms which are balanced to cost more because they can be activated later considerably worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}